  "question": {
    "text": "Ionisation energy of $\\mathrm{He}^{+}$is $19.6 \\times 10^{-18} \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{atom}^{-1}$. The energy of the first stationary state $(\\mathrm{n}=1)$ of $\\mathrm{Li}^{2+}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$4.41 \\times 10^{-16} \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{atom}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-4.41 \\times 10^{-17} \\mathrm{~J}_{\\text {atom }}{ }^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-2.2 \\times 10^{-15} \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{atom}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$8.82 \\times 10^{-17} \\mathrm{~J}_{\\text {atom }^{-1}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\mathrm{IE}_{\\mathrm{He}^{+}}=13.6 \\mathrm{Z}_{\\mathrm{He}^{+}}^2\\left[\\frac{1}{1^2}-\\frac{1}{\\infty^2}\\right]=13.6 \\mathrm{Z}_{\\mathrm{He}^{+}}^2 \\text { where }\\left(\\mathrm{Z}_{\\mathrm{He}^{+}}=2\\right)\n$$\nHence $13.6 \\times Z_{\\mathrm{He}^{+}}^2=19.6 \\times 10^{-18} \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{atom}^{-1}$.\n$$\n\\left(\\mathrm{E}_1\\right)_{\\mathrm{L}^{+2}}=-13.6 \\mathrm{Z}_{\\mathrm{Uj}^{+2}}^2 \\times \\frac{1}{1^2}=-13.6 \\mathrm{Z}_{\\mathrm{He}^{+}}^2 \\times\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{Z}_{\\mathrm{L}^{+2}}^2}{\\mathrm{Z}_{\\mathrm{He}^{+}}^2}\\right]=-19.6 \\times 10^{-18} \\times \\frac{9}{4}=-4.41 \\times 10^{-17} \\mathrm{~J} / \\text { atom }\n$$"
  }
